[38.728324, "o", "(s) so far\r\n  │ Now let me verify it works:\r\n[approval] bash: pip3 --version 2>&1 — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash pip3 --version 2>&1\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  qwen3.6-35b — 15 tool call(s) so far\r\n[approval] bash: python3 -m pip --version 2>&1 — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash python3 -m pip --version 2>&1\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  qwen3.6-35b — 16 tool call(s) so far\r\npip is fully restored. Here's what was wrong and what I did:\r\n\r\n**Problem:** The `pip` package files were missing from `/usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/` — only the `pip-24.3.1.dist-info` metadata directory remained. The `pip3` binary existed but couldn't import the `pip` module, so every `pip install` failed with `ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'pip'`.\r\n\r\n**Fix:** Extracted the bundled pip wheel (`/usr/local/lib/python3.13/ensurepip/_bundled/pip-24.3.1-py3-none-any.whl`) directly into `site-packages/`. This restored the full pip package including all `_internal` and `_vendor` subpackages.\r\n\r\nBoth `pip3` and `python3 -m pip` now work"]
[38.728328, "o", " correctly.\r\n\r\n[refusal] role=implementor model=qwen3.6-35b tools=16 surface=801f9f2a7a86\r\n"]
